@startuml
' This UML source uses PlantUML format.
' https://plantuml.com/sequence-diagram for syntax details.
!theme minty
master -> feature
'help themes

' Optional styles
'skinparam monochrome reverse
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam SequenceMessageAlign direction
skinparam shadowing false
'skinparam handwritten true
skinparam roundcorner 30
autonumber

title GreenPay git-flow

participant master
participant release
participant develop
participant "GPAY-123" as task

== Начало работы над задачей ==

master -> feature: create a branch as a fork from "master"
feature -> task: create a branch as a fork from feature branch
task -> task: push commits locally, technical commits allowed


== Основная работа закончена, отдаем на код-ревью ==

task -> feature: PR with rebase (squash on github)
note right of feature
	Rebase (squash) is optional for history cleanup.
	Try to avoid technical comimits in feature branch.
	Only useful "feature" commits should be passed.

	Unit developers should approve
	the changes to feature branch.
end note


== Move to QA on unit ==

feature -> release99: merge

note right of release99
	For tests on unit
	you could push feature branch
	directly to "release99".
end note


== Optional debugging on unit ==

release99 -> release99: optional technical commits & pushes

note right of release99
	Any technical commits for debugging allowed.
	Direct pushes without PRs.
end note


== The case when more commits should be added to task ==

task -> task: commit & push
task -> feature: PR to task
feature -> release99: merge and test again

note right of feature
	The important thing is that "release99"  **must not** be merged to
	any other branches! It only accepts merges for testing on unit env.
end note

== Optional cleanup unit for testing another feature ==

master -> release99: replace with master after for branch cleanup

note left of release99
	At this point we get clean "release99"
	that could be used for other features testing.

	But this way could be dangerous
	for migrations consistency :|
end note

== Release the feature ==

feature -> develop: merge with PR (no rebase allowed!)
develop -> master: merge for new release (no rebase allowed!)

@enduml
